                  "content": "SELECTED: candidate_04\n\nCONFIDENCE: HIGH\n\nEXPLANATION:\nThe fix commit changes CmsRenderTemplate.java line 187 from\n`loader.getResources(\"cmsFreemarkerTransforms\")` back to\n`loader.getResources(\"cmsFreemarkerTransforms.properties\")`, restoring the\n\".properties\" extension that the classloader resource lookup requires to find\nthe actual file (config/cmsFreemarkerTransforms.properties, created originally\nin candidate_01).\n\nTracing the history of this exact line across the candidates:\n- candidate_01 introduces the file `cmsFreemarkerTransforms.properties` and the\n  original correct call `loader.getResources(\"cmsFreemarkerTransforms.properties\")`.\n- candidate_04 performs a broad refactor that strips the \".properties\" suffix\n  from resource/property names used with `UtilProperties.getPropertyValue`/\n  `getPropertyAsBoolean` (e.g. \"cms.properties\" -> \"cms\"), which is correct for\n  those UtilProperties calls since that API expects the base name without the\n  extension. However, this same refactor incorrectly also applied the same\n  transformation to the unrelated `loader.getResources(...)` call in\n  CmsRenderTemplate.java, changing it from\n  `\"cmsFreemarkerTransforms.properties\"` to `\"cmsFreemarkerTransforms\"`. Since\n  `ClassLoader.getResources` does a raw resource-path lookup (not going through\n  UtilProperties' implicit \".properties\" resolution), this broke the lookup of\n  the actual file and introduced the bug described in the fix (\"cms: fix\n  .properties extension bug\").\n- candidate_05 is identical to the fix commit diff itself (same before/after\n  blob hashes as fix_commit_diff.txt), reverting the change back to\n  `\"cmsFreemarkerTransforms.properties\"`. This is the fix, not the\n  bug-introducing commit.\n\nTherefore candidate_04 is the commit that introduced the bug by mistakenly\nstripping the \".properties\" extension from a raw classloader resource lookup\nduring an otherwise-legitimate refactor of UtilProperties calls.\n"
                }
              }
            ]
